Let’s denote the entries of $A$ as $A_{ij}$, and the entries of $B = A - A^t$ are: $$
B_{ij} = A_{ij} - A_{ji}
$$

So: $$
B = \begin{bmatrix} 0 & B_{12} \\ -B_{12} & 0 \end{bmatrix}
$$

So: $$
\mathbb{E}[\det(B)] = \mathbb{E}[B_{12}^2] = \frac{1}{2}
$$

Now, it turns out that for such a random skew-symmetric matrix, the expected value of the determinant is: $$
\boxed{0}
$$

### ✅ Final Answer: $$
\boxed{\mathbb{E}[\det(A - A^t)] = 0}
$$
